<title>UK: UK's Clarke and George to meet Wednesday morning.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke and George to meet Wednesday morning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke and Bank of England Governor Eddie George will hold their monthly meeting on UK monetary policy on Wednesday morning, official sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a morning meeting, beyond that we do not know,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>Traders said they would watch closely the Bank of England's money market operations around 1200 GMT tomorrow, for an indication that monetary policy has been shifted.</p>
</text>
